1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:15,390
[Bret] One of the most intimate ways
to kill someone

2
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:17,142
is to push them from a great height.

3
00:00:17,226 --> 00:00:19,478
[♪ "Vienna" playing]

4
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:23,315
[Bret] Terminal velocity refers
to the maximum speed

5
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:26,193
attainable by a human body falling
through midair.

6
00:00:26,902 --> 00:00:29,112
It takes roughly 12 seconds
to achieve that speed.

7
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:31,198
♪ We walked in the cold air ♪

8
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:35,369
[Bret] Terry never even got close
before he collided

9
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,287
with the hardwood of the Schaffers' foyer.

10
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,415
♪ Freezing breath on a windowpane… ♪

11
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:42,960
[Bret] Looking back on that fall semester
of senior year,

12
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:45,629
there was no shortage
of traumatizing developments.

13
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:49,174
The serial killer, or various killers
terrorizing our school,

14
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:51,593
the fracturing of our friend group,

15
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:55,180
and the untimely deaths of teenagers
who had no business dying.

16
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:59,476
But to this day,
the two questions that still beguile

17
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,228
and disturb me the most are:

18
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:05,274
Who pushed Terry Schaffer
over that stairway banister?

19
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:07,150
And why?

20
00:01:07,234 --> 00:01:08,235
[no audible dialogue]

21
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:10,529
[Bret] Many people assumed it was me.

22
00:01:11,113 --> 00:01:12,823
Terry had betrayed me.

23
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:14,575
Not only had he taken advantage of me

24
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:16,785
at the Beverly Hills Hotel,
but I believed then,

25
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:21,832
as now, that he had videotaped us
as some sort of perverse insurance policy.

26
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:27,254
♪ This means nothing to me… ♪

27
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:31,008
[Bret] The truth is,
by the night of Debbie's Halloween party,

28
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:34,136
seemingly everyone had a reason
to want Terry Schaffer dead.

29
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:38,515
Steven had worked loyally for Terry
for a decade.

30
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:41,560
And Terry had repaid him
by routinely humiliating him

31
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:43,854
and thwarting his efforts
to produce a movie.

32
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:52,362
♪ Freezing breath on a windowpane… ♪

33
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:55,032
[Bret] Liz had endured years
of Terry's infidelity

34
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:57,826
and exceedingly sloppy lies
about his sexuality.

35
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:01,663
All the while something malevolent
had been gestating inside her.

36
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:04,291
♪ A man in the dark in a picture frame ♪

37
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:07,127
♪ So mystic and soulful… ♪

38
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:10,172
[Bret] And the dormancy period
was finally over.

39
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:13,842
Then there was Debbie.

40
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:17,846
Daddy's little girl had lost faith in
the first and only man she'd ever trust.

41
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,933
Her rage was compounded by a profound…

42
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:24,728
♪ The feeling has gone, only you and I ♪

43
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:29,024
♪ It means nothing to me ♪

44
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:30,651
[Bret] …almost biological hurt.

45
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:35,364
♪ This means nothing to me ♪

46
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:37,324
♪ Oh, Vienna… ♪

47
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:40,661
[Bret] Susan despised Terry
for ruining Debbie's life

48
00:02:40,744 --> 00:02:43,205
and hated him even more
for trying to ruin mine.

49
00:02:48,377 --> 00:02:53,507
Susan, I would discover much later,
had learned about my secret shame.

50
00:02:55,384 --> 00:02:58,720
Thom had been acting increasingly
violent and erratic that year.

51
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:00,180
♪ The music is weaving ♪

52
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:03,058
[Bret] And harbored an intense grudge
against his own father.

53
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,144
Or any father figure.

54
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:09,856
♪ Haunting notes, pizzicato strings ♪

55
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,858
♪ The rhythm is calling ♪

56
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:18,824
[Bret] And of course, there was Robert,
a known psychopath.

57
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:21,368
♪ Alone in the night
As the daylight brings… ♪

58
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:23,370
[Bret] The circumstances
of his own mother's death

59
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,747
were eerily similar
to those of Terry's fall.

60
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,795
From the moment I first looked in his eyes
at that matinee of The Shining…

61
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:38,301
I knew that he possessed the ability
and desire to commit unspeakable evil.

62
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:45,142
♪ The image has gone, only you and I ♪

63
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,894
♪ It means nothing to me ♪

64
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:50,814
[Bret] We all fantasized
about harming Terry.

65
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:54,109
♪ This means nothing to me ♪

66
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:57,070
[Bret] But only one of us was capable
of actually doing it.

67
00:03:57,154 --> 00:04:00,240
♪ Oh, Vienna ♪

68
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:21,678
[♪ eerie music playing]

69
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,984
[indistinct chattering on TV]

70
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:44,910
[exhales deeply]

71
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:46,995
[person grunts on TV]

72
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:51,333
[Terry] I know… I know he…
he pulled a hair out of your head.

73
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:52,417
It was barbaric.

74
00:04:52,501 --> 00:04:56,254
But I am putting together this picture
that you, Polanski…

75
00:04:56,338 --> 00:04:58,548
The dream team. It works.

76
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,759
You guys are a magical combination.

77
00:05:01,343 --> 00:05:02,761
[Debbie] Get off the phone.

78
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:05,263
I'm just talking to Faye Dunaway.
Give me a minute.

79
00:05:05,347 --> 00:05:06,556
Fuck Faye Dunaway.

80
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,475
I said get off the phone now.

81
00:05:09,351 --> 00:05:10,852
This is important.

82
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,898
Faye, can I call you back?

83
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:18,151
Five minutes. Okay, bye.

84
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,197
-What?
-[door closes]

85
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:27,369
We suddenly find ourselves
in a bit of a pickle, Terry.

86
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,830
Why did you call me that?

87
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:31,498
-I'm Daddy.
-Not anymore.

88
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:36,336
Or should I say
I'm not Daddy's little girl anymore.

89
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,005
I always knew this day would come.

90
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:41,675
You're pregnant. That's okay.

91
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,552
-We can take care of it.
-I'm not pregnant.

92
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:46,596
I've been practicing the pull-out method
since I was 16.

93
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,182
No, no. Don't say that.

94
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:50,559
Don't talk to me like that.

95
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:52,602
I did not raise you to speak that way.

96
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:57,941
I've come across some information
about you.

97
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:59,901
What's that supposed to mean?

98
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:03,530
Think long and hard
about what I could possibly know.

99
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:07,450
What is the worst thing
I could find out about you?

100
00:06:08,952 --> 00:06:10,078
Well…

101
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,082
at long last.

102
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:15,709
I always suspected.

103
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:18,378
And I finally found out.

104
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:22,799
What did you find out?

105
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,136
Are you threatening me?

106
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:36,479
Let it suffice to say
that some information has come

107
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:41,902
across my pink princess desk
that could absolutely be your downfall.

108
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:44,821
I could tell Mommy.

109
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:48,033
I could call the studio.

110
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:51,828
I could call the press,
but I've decided I won't.

111
00:06:52,704 --> 00:06:59,419
If, starting today, you give me
exactly what I want, what I'm entitled to.

112
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:01,171
Stop it. Stop it right now.

113
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,882
Or what? You'll ground me?

114
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:06,092
Has it ever worked? I always snuck out.

115
00:07:06,635 --> 00:07:07,636
[scoffs]

116
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:13,850
You know, I used to resent you so much
when you'd get mad at me.

117
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:17,687
Whenever I lost a contest
or a game of Monopoly,

118
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:22,901
you'd say to me, "Debbie,
you are just like your mother." [scoffs]

119
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:24,277
I knew that was code for loser.

120
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:26,321
I hated you for that.

121
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:31,826
But the truth is,
I'm more like you than her.

122
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:35,747
-I always have been.
-You are nothing like me.

123
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,208
Like you, Daddy, I'm a killer.

124
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:40,835
I inherited that quality from you.

125
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:44,005
I don't like my car.

126
00:07:44,089 --> 00:07:45,632
I want a Ferrari.

127
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:48,301
I don't want to go to college.

128
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:50,095
I want to be a star.

129
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:54,349
And you will arrange a screen test for me

130
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:57,018
and get me that star-making part.

131
00:07:57,769 --> 00:08:00,730
-Am I clear?
-You have no talent.

132
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,232
But I have information.

133
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:07,779
I am now aware of something
that Mommy could never prove.

134
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:11,116
Look into my eyes.

135
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:16,162
You know I finally know now.

136
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:23,878
This is just the beginning of a long list
of requests I'll be coming to you with.

137
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:26,005
Nice talk.

138
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,091
Good times.

139
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:33,221
What? What do you know?

140
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:34,639
Tell me right now!

141
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:37,434
Get your hands off me.

142
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:43,148
You wouldn't want to bruise
your shiniest trophy now, would you?

143
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,941
[scoffs]

144
00:08:47,152 --> 00:08:48,278
I know.

145
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:51,948
I will tell.

146
00:08:53,408 --> 00:08:55,201
It could all go up in a puff of smoke,

147
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:58,621
and that's your greatest fear, isn't it?

148
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:04,377
I can't tell you how wonderful it feels

149
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:06,880
to finally win.

150
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:11,676
To finally, in the end, get what I want.

151
00:09:18,141 --> 00:09:19,142
[door opens]

152
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,942
[quiet chattering]

153
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:30,028
[♪ pop music playing on speakers]

154
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:54,344
[Thom] How are you?

155
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:57,222
I'm late for tennis with Debbie.

156
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,015
What did you want to talk about?

157
00:09:59,641 --> 00:10:00,850
I fucked up.

158
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:02,477
I know that.

159
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:06,523
-I was too intense.
-You threatened me with a knife.

160
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:10,735
The same week our classmate's
severed head was found in a trophy case.

161
00:10:10,819 --> 00:10:14,239
So I picked the wrong week
to threaten my girlfriend with a knife.

162
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:16,116
Thom, this isn't funny.

163
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,702
Is there a connection there, by the way?

164
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:23,248
Between your obsession with knives
and what happened to Matt?

165
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:25,959
My obsession with knives?

166
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:28,169
What are you talking about?

167
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:31,381
You're like a different person lately.

168
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:34,300
-I don't even know you.
-You don't know me?

169
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:37,595
I know you.

170
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:39,931
I know you're scared.

171
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:43,143
I know you need somebody to protect you.

172
00:10:44,227 --> 00:10:45,687
It's what you said.

173
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:47,897
Kids are dying.

174
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:53,987
We're not safe in LA.
We're surrounded by very, very bad people.

175
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,446
Like Robert.

176
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:57,699
[inhales]

177
00:10:57,782 --> 00:11:00,201
There's something seriously wrong
with him, don't you think?

178
00:11:00,285 --> 00:11:02,829
No, Thom, I don't think.

179
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:06,708
Because I've never seen Robert
do anything half as disturbing

180
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:10,128
as threatening to slice his veins open
with a steak knife.

181
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,507
[♪ intense music playing]

182
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:27,770
What's that?

183
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:31,024
I spoke to the school guidance counselor
about you.

184
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:34,444
She said it can be really hard
for teenagers these days

185
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:39,032
with all the pressures
of college applications and divorce.

186
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,492
And the stuff with your dad.

187
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:43,995
You spoke to somebody about my dad?

188
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:47,123
You should not have done that, Susan.
You really should not have done that.

189
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:49,000
-Do you understand me?
-That.

190
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:53,630
That is the look in your eyes that
makes me wonder what you're capable of.

191
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,465
I have so much to live for.

192
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:57,592
You.

193
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:01,179
Our family, our future.

194
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,388
You…

195
00:12:04,349 --> 00:12:06,059
Thom, what the fuck are you doing?

196
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,227
[whispers] Su…

197
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:10,730
Thom, I just… I need you to sit back down.

198
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:14,692
-Susan Marie Reynolds.
-Oh.

199
00:12:19,197 --> 00:12:21,032
I want to protect you.

200
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:25,036
I… I…

201
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:27,872
-I want to marry you.
-[gasps]

202
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:31,584
I want to hold you in my arms
until you fall asleep.

203
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:38,549
And once you're asleep, I'll stay awake
and I'll hold you all night long.

204
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:43,096
That's the only way
that I can be sure that you'll be safe.

205
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:47,892
Um…

206
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:51,229
Thom, what are you doing on the ground?
Did Susan lose an earring?

207
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:54,899
We are late for tennis, and I have to stop
at home to change out my purse.

208
00:12:54,983 --> 00:12:56,818
So let's go.

209
00:12:57,402 --> 00:12:59,445
[Susan breathes shakily]

210
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:03,241
Think about it.

211
00:13:04,284 --> 00:13:05,743
What the fuck was that?

212
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:10,790
Thom reminding me why I broke up with him.

213
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,583
Oh, God, our boyfriends suck.

214
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:15,628
-Ex-boyfriend.
-Oh, whatever.

215
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:19,257
It's senior year.
There's no excuse not to have fun.

216
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:22,010
Especially the week of Halloween.
My favorite holiday.

217
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:25,513
[chuckles, sniffles] You're right,
we could all use a distraction,

218
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:29,058
but the police have basically canceled
everything because of The Trawler.

219
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:32,895
[Bret] Much to my relief,
The Trawler's gruesome acts

220
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:35,606
had finally permeated the psyche
of my friends.

221
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:40,445
…the like are gripped in terror as
a serial killer known as The Trawler

222
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:45,491
targets students at an elite prep school
in California's San Fernando Valley.

223
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:49,370
[Bret] I was no longer some crazy
Cassandra spewing hollow warnings.

224
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:50,580
Now everyone was afraid.

225
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,876
The Trawler murder spree
had become national news.

226
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,628
The killer's elevated
public profile seemed

227
00:13:57,712 --> 00:14:00,048
to please and maybe even excite him.

228
00:14:00,131 --> 00:14:03,885
It seemed he liked the attention and
soon started seeking it out more directly.

229
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:07,972
In a letter received by the editorial
board of the Los Angeles Times,

230
00:14:08,056 --> 00:14:11,517
an individual who identified himself
as The Trawler

231
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:14,270
issued specific and credible threats.

232
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:19,484
Now the disturbing communiqué promises to,
quote, "slaughter all the kiddies

233
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:22,028
in their costumes
going trick-or-treating."

234
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:24,572
[Bret] At that point,
I had repeatedly told the police

235
00:14:24,655 --> 00:14:26,949
that the person responsible was Robert.

236
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:30,244
Why were they sitting
on the identity of The Trawler?

237
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:34,665
What strings had Robert's wealthy
and well-connected family pulled?

238
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,711
He had already gotten away
with murder once back in Chicago.

239
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:43,049
I was determined now, more than ever,

240
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:45,343
to not let him get away with it again.

241
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,220
I knew Robert's secret.

242
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:49,138
The problem was…

243
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:52,350
he also knew mine.

244
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:57,063
My plan was to confront him on Halloween.

245
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,649
This time I wouldn't be seduced
by his charm.

246
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,820
Or overwhelmed by my own desire.

247
00:15:04,862 --> 00:15:07,949
We were all going to
a sort of safe house party,

248
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:10,535
but I knew none of us would be safe
until Robert Mallory

249
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:12,286
was out of our lives forever.

250
