two months into our senior year.

507
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:49,353
I observed this from afar,

508
00:28:49,436 --> 00:28:53,565
and it hurt me deeply,
this newfound distance.

509
00:28:53,649 --> 00:28:54,858
I'm so, so sorry.

510
00:28:55,442 --> 00:28:58,987
No one should ever have to deal with that,
some fucking horse head in a bed.

511
00:28:59,071 --> 00:29:00,072
[Susan] Mmm.

512
00:29:01,114 --> 00:29:02,449
Who do you think did it?

513
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,077
I don't know.

514
00:29:06,036 --> 00:29:08,997
But I felt like I was living
in one of those horror movies

515
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:10,958
that Bret used to drag me to.

516
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:13,460
I don't even like those kinds of movies.

517
00:29:14,044 --> 00:29:15,420
I like love stories.

518
00:29:15,504 --> 00:29:16,672
[both laughing]

519
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:17,965
Me too.

520
00:29:19,675 --> 00:29:22,761
[Bret] I used to be the one
that she poured her heart out to.

521
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:24,888
But not anymore.

522
00:29:25,889 --> 00:29:29,267
Now she turned exclusively
to Robert Mallory.

523
00:29:29,351 --> 00:29:30,352
[no audible dialogue]

524
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:34,272
[Bret] It wasn't until years later,
after all the death and tragedy,

525
00:29:34,356 --> 00:29:37,192
that I learned how Robert had
wormed his way into her confidence.

526
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:39,403
Thom is just… He's not the same.

527
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:41,238
He's changed. He's…

528
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:42,406
Erratic.

529
00:29:43,156 --> 00:29:44,199
Yeah.

530
00:29:44,282 --> 00:29:45,701
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

531
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,995
Once when we were drunk, he told me,

532
00:29:48,078 --> 00:29:51,999
"Susan, if I can't have you,
then nobody else can."

533
00:29:52,082 --> 00:29:53,583
You're not a possession.

534
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:54,668
I know.

535
00:29:55,502 --> 00:29:58,005
Yeah, and Bret is…

536
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:00,674
Bret's just…

537
00:30:00,757 --> 00:30:03,510
He's different now.
I don't feel like I can trust him.

538
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:06,138
-Why not?
-[groans]

539
00:30:06,221 --> 00:30:08,890
I don't know why I'm telling you this,
but… [sniffles]

540
00:30:08,974 --> 00:30:11,685
…at the stables,
right before school started,

541
00:30:12,394 --> 00:30:16,023
Bret said that Spirit was stupid.

542
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:17,399
[chuckles]

543
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:19,067
He hated that horse.

544
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:21,528
Like he was jealous?

545
00:30:24,031 --> 00:30:25,032
Yeah.

546
00:30:25,115 --> 00:30:28,493
[Bret] The web Robert Mallory weaved
around Susan,

547
00:30:28,577 --> 00:30:30,370
I found out in time,

548
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:35,625
was based on a simple rule of manipulation
only a sociopath would know at 18.

549
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,588
Never demand.

550
00:30:40,756 --> 00:30:42,591
Never push too hard.

551
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:46,845
Let them come to you.

552
00:30:49,181 --> 00:30:51,767
Always let them come to you first.

553
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:05,781
Yeah.

554
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:07,407
-[Susan] Mmm?
-A little bit…

555
00:31:07,491 --> 00:31:09,117
[both chuckle]

556
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:16,875
Susan, it pains me to say this,

557
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:21,254
but… I think you have to acknowledge
that you might have outgrown your friends.

558
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:24,091
But I love them.

559
00:31:24,174 --> 00:31:26,176
People change, you know.

560
00:31:26,259 --> 00:31:28,637
And this is the kind of time
when it starts to happen.

561
00:31:31,765 --> 00:31:34,935
-Bret hates me. [chuckling] I know.
-[laughs] Yeah.

562
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:37,145
He's jealous or something.

563
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:40,107
And Thom and I have…

564
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:43,693
a complicated relationship.

565
00:31:46,363 --> 00:31:48,031
Why is it complicated?

566
00:31:51,368 --> 00:31:53,495
Because we're both in love
with the same girl.

567
00:31:59,543 --> 00:32:03,130
We shouldn't rush into anything, you know?
We should be cool.

568
00:32:03,213 --> 00:32:05,340
I know you don't want to hurt anyone,
and I don't either.

569
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:09,219
But the future is so bright.

570
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:13,682
It's right over the horizon,
waiting for us.

571
00:32:16,059 --> 00:32:17,435
If we both want it.

572
00:32:28,155 --> 00:32:29,656
[Bret] That fateful night,

573
00:32:29,739 --> 00:32:32,826
before the most terrifying
event of her life occurred,

574
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:38,331
Susan Reynolds went to bed feeling
what she hadn't felt for months.

575
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,041
Peace.

576
00:32:40,125 --> 00:32:42,127
[phone ringing]

577
00:32:43,545 --> 00:32:45,547
[Bret] And then
that feeling of safety was shattered.

578
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,841
[ringing continues]

579
00:32:49,968 --> 00:32:52,053
Hello. [inhales]

580
00:32:52,888 --> 00:32:56,558
[person breathing heavily]

581
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:17,162
[♪ eerie music playing]

582
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:29,591
[sighs]

583
00:33:35,055 --> 00:33:36,640
[floor creaking]

584
00:33:44,481 --> 00:33:46,691
[breathing shakily]

585
00:33:53,949 --> 00:33:55,533
[door hinges squeaking]

586
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:08,004
[door slamming]

587
00:34:09,506 --> 00:34:12,634
[screaming]

588
00:34:21,393 --> 00:34:22,394
[grunts]

589
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:29,401
-[screams, gasps]
-[door thuds]

590
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:31,528
-[screaming]
-[doorknob rattling]

591
00:34:35,699 --> 00:34:37,784
[hyperventilating]

592
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:40,912
-[screaming]
-[person] Let me in, let me in! Come on!

593
00:34:40,996 --> 00:34:42,747
[doorknob rattling]

594
00:34:42,831 --> 00:34:44,207
It's Thom!

595
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,377
Thom? [panting]

596
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:59,598
Hey. Hey. Hey. It's okay, it's okay.

597
00:34:59,681 --> 00:35:02,267
-It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.
-[crying] No. No!

598
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:03,351
I was worried about you.

599
00:35:03,435 --> 00:35:05,937
I was watching you from outside
and I saw him.

600
00:35:06,021 --> 00:35:09,899
I saw him attacking you, so I broke in,
and I raced up and I fought him.

601
00:35:09,983 --> 00:35:12,444
-I fought him off. Look, I fought him off.
-[panting]

602
00:35:12,527 --> 00:35:16,114
What… What… What… What happened?

603
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:18,116
I pushed him.
I pushed him off the balcony.

604
00:35:20,994 --> 00:35:23,163
[panting]

605
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,958
[unlocks door]

606
00:35:39,596 --> 00:35:40,930
Where is he?

607
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:43,016
[♪ eerie music playing]

608
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:49,022
I don't know.

609
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:54,611
[Susan inhales shakily]

610
00:35:55,904 --> 00:35:56,988
[gulps]

611
00:36:03,453 --> 00:36:05,789
[Bret] Debbie had somehow
persuaded her father

612
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:08,917
to throw her
the most epic Halloween party of all time.

613
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:12,545
The theme of the event was "Unmasked,"
which was ironic,

614
00:36:12,629 --> 00:36:13,963
because by the end of the night,

615
00:36:14,047 --> 00:36:17,342
many, if not all, of our secrets
were going to come out.

616
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:23,473
Debbie demanded
we all wear no masks and black tie.

617
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:25,475
So I rented one.

618
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:30,730
I remember the cavernous emptiness
of my house that afternoon.

619
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:32,982
It was the first time
since I was a little kid

620
00:36:33,066 --> 00:36:35,110
that I remember missing my father.

621
00:36:36,027 --> 00:36:39,239
My father used to tie my bow ties
for school dances.

622
00:36:40,532 --> 00:36:43,410
It was a skill to this day
I have not mastered.

623
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,663
Standing there in my bedroom,

624
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:50,166
hours away from my first real
adult black-tie party,

625
00:36:51,126 --> 00:36:52,669
I had never felt so old.

626
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:55,755
I had also never felt so vulnerable.

627
00:36:56,464 --> 00:36:58,341
Trick-or-treating in sixth grade
with the gang

628
00:36:58,425 --> 00:37:00,218
felt like a dream from a past life.

629
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:01,344
[doorbell rings]

630
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:05,557
[kids] Trick or treat!

631
00:37:13,106 --> 00:37:16,860
[Bret] I was homesick for a time and place
that didn't exist anymore.

632
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,951
And would never exist again.

633
00:37:25,869 --> 00:37:27,996
[♪ "Only a Lad" playing]

634
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:29,622
[partygoers chattering]

635
00:37:54,773 --> 00:37:58,401
♪ Johnny was bad, even as a child
Everybody could tell ♪

636
00:38:00,028 --> 00:38:03,907
♪ Everyone said if you don't get straight
You'll surely go to hell… ♪

637
00:38:04,741 --> 00:38:06,201
The only thing I can't figure out

638
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,287
is how you got out
of that killer costume so fast.

639
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:11,206
How can you say that?

640
00:38:11,289 --> 00:38:13,875
It wasn't me. I rescued you.

641
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:15,960
I know it was you, Thom.

642
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:19,714
And I haven't told anyone
because I have been trying to protect you.

643
00:38:19,798 --> 00:38:20,799
Even now.

644
00:38:21,758 --> 00:38:23,676
But, tonight, that all ends.

645
00:38:25,512 --> 00:38:27,263
♪ He liked to burn things… ♪

646
00:38:27,972 --> 00:38:29,933
I know it was you, Steven.

647
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:32,977
I know you're the one who videotaped me.

648
00:38:33,061 --> 00:38:35,772
[clicks tongue] Trick or treat, dumpling.

649
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:41,236
What do you say to a quick dip
in the Jacuzzi out in the dojo?

650
00:38:41,861 --> 00:38:43,613
Never say no to a hot tub.

651
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:48,368
I wanna say…

652
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:51,496
I'm sorry.

653
00:38:51,579 --> 00:38:53,790
I know you loved that horse.

654
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,626
I understand what he meant to you.

655
00:38:57,710 --> 00:39:01,464
And I promise that we will find out
who did that to him.

656
00:39:01,548 --> 00:39:03,091
We all know Daddy did it.

657
00:39:04,634 --> 00:39:06,469
Or his insurance company.

658
00:39:08,263 --> 00:39:10,348
Daddy's much darker than you think.

659
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:15,436
I wanna say I'm sorry too.

660
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,564
I understand now
just how much you've gone through

661
00:39:17,647 --> 00:39:19,065
over the years.

662
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:22,819
How difficult it must have been
keeping so many secrets.

663
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:37,417
[♪ mysterious music playing]

664
00:39:44,924 --> 00:39:46,217
[inhales]

665
00:40:07,572 --> 00:40:08,990
Your hair's wet.

666
00:40:10,575 --> 00:40:12,702
-Were you in the hot tub?
-Yeah.

667
00:40:14,037 --> 00:40:16,956
It was all quite… enlightening.

668
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:19,167
Informative.

669
00:40:21,586 --> 00:40:22,587
Let me help you.

670
00:40:32,931 --> 00:40:34,599
I think we should talk…

671
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:38,770
about what happened between us.

672
00:40:39,687 --> 00:40:41,522
What happened between us?

673
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:43,858
You know…

674
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:46,945
you came over.

675
00:40:48,571 --> 00:40:50,281
What the fuck are you talking about?

676
00:40:53,159 --> 00:40:54,577
God. So cliché.

677
00:40:55,203 --> 00:40:57,830
Straight guy pretends
that it never happened.

678
00:40:58,623 --> 00:40:59,999
Okay, dude.

679
00:41:00,083 --> 00:41:03,127
You were never in my bed
just like you were never at The Shining.

680
00:41:03,753 --> 00:41:06,297
You're obsessed with me,
and I'm tired of it.

681
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:08,591
Who cares if I saw some movie a year ago?

682
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:10,927
I do, Robert.

683
00:41:11,636 --> 00:41:14,555
-So did Katherine Latchford.
-Who?

684
00:41:14,639 --> 00:41:17,266
The girl that you saw it with
and then murdered.

685
00:41:18,267 --> 00:41:20,979
I met your aunt. She told me.

686
00:41:21,062 --> 00:41:24,649
My aunt? Auntie Abby?
She's a depressive alcoholic.

687
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:28,152
She asked to meet with me
and told me everything.

688
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:32,115
You were at The Shining that day.
She said you were dangerous.

689
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:34,283
She said that you were a fucking psycho.

690
00:41:34,367 --> 00:41:38,955
You know, everything that I ever suspected
about you, Robert, turned out to be true.

691
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:40,707
Everything.

692
00:41:40,790 --> 00:41:43,418
You killed Katherine Latchford,
and Matt Kellner,

693
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:46,713
and your mom,
and probably many, many others.

694
00:41:46,796 --> 00:41:49,966
My aunt barely has the coherence
to cash her alimony checks.

695
00:41:50,049 --> 00:41:51,050
[Bret scoffs]

696
00:41:52,719 --> 00:41:55,555
Listen. Look, Bret,

697
00:41:55,638 --> 00:41:57,515
I have empathy for you.

698
00:41:58,933 --> 00:42:01,102
You're struggling with your sexuality.

699
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:05,189
And from what I've read,
Death in Venice, among other things,

700
00:42:05,898 --> 00:42:07,608
that's some really heavy shit.

701
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:10,403
I feel bad for you.

702
00:42:11,237 --> 00:42:12,488
I really do.

703
00:42:14,407 --> 00:42:16,993
You have to get over this little crush
that you have on me.

704
00:42:17,785 --> 00:42:18,995
[Bret chuckles]

705
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:22,040
I hope you find somebody. Really, I do.

706
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:26,878
And now that I have Susan,
I know how important it is.

707
00:42:27,462 --> 00:42:30,256
You know, love.

708
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:31,924
What are you talking about?

709
00:42:32,008 --> 00:42:34,093
Susan and I are together.

710
00:42:35,428 --> 00:42:36,637
She's with me.

711
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:39,390
Not Thom, not you.

712
00:42:39,474 --> 00:42:40,558
Bullshit.

713
00:42:42,018 --> 00:42:43,603
That's bullshit. That…

714
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:50,485
I won't let that happen.
You will not have Susan.

715
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:53,613
-I will die before I let that happen.
-Do you promise?

716
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:54,697
[scoffs]

717
00:42:54,781 --> 00:42:58,034
You know what, Robert?
You should know, it's over.

718
00:42:58,618 --> 00:43:00,078
You're done.

719
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:01,954
I have a meeting
with the detectives tomorrow

720
00:43:02,038 --> 00:43:03,915
to tell them everything I know about you.

721
00:43:04,499 --> 00:43:05,833
The Katherine Latchford story.

722
00:43:07,043 --> 00:43:08,336
Everything.

723
00:43:09,045 --> 00:43:10,088
Congratulations.

724
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:11,422
You're about to join Ted Bundy

725
00:43:11,506 --> 00:43:13,841
in the handsome serial killer
hall of fame.

726
00:43:16,511 --> 00:43:18,179
Let me go to the police
with you tomorrow, Bret.

727
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,389
There's some things
I'd like to share with them about you.

728
00:43:20,473 --> 00:43:21,682
Get your hands off of me.

729
00:43:21,766 --> 00:43:23,684
I called your father's place of work

730
00:43:23,768 --> 00:43:27,021
to inquire about his mysterious
months-long disappearance.

731
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:29,273
-They're on vacation. You know that.
-Really?

732
00:43:29,357 --> 00:43:31,859
'Cause they told me he never told them
he was going on vacation.

733
00:43:31,943 --> 00:43:34,278
One day, he just didn't show up.

734
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:36,739
They presumed he quit.

735
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:42,370
Is he on a permanent getaway
with your mother in the basement, Bret?

736
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:43,454
Did you hack them to pieces

737
00:43:43,538 --> 00:43:45,331
and store them down there
with the root vegetables?

738
00:43:45,414 --> 00:43:47,917
Did you bury them in the backyard?
Did you kill them?

739
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:50,044
Fuck you! That's a lie.

740
00:43:50,670 --> 00:43:53,339
[laughs] I think you're sick!

741
00:43:54,257 --> 00:43:57,343
You're a sad, little novelist
with writer's block.

742
00:43:58,094 --> 00:44:00,138
You're killing all these kids
and trying to frame it on me.

743
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:01,889
That way, you can write what you know.

744
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:05,726
Quite the bestseller in the making.
You can finish it in prison.

745
00:44:07,728 --> 00:44:08,896
What's going on here?

746
00:44:08,980 --> 00:44:10,064
Hey, babe.

747
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:13,693
I was just helping Bret with his bow tie.

748
00:44:14,485 --> 00:44:16,279
Bret, can I talk to you for a minute?

749
00:44:16,362 --> 00:44:19,031
No, that's okay, babe.
I think I'm all caught up.

750
00:44:23,870 --> 00:44:27,415
Guys, hop to it. Oingo Boingo's
already started their second encore.

751
00:44:40,011 --> 00:44:42,513
[♪ mysterious music playing]

752
00:44:51,147 --> 00:44:53,316
[phone ringing]

753
00:44:58,279 --> 00:44:59,280
Hello.

754
00:45:04,994 --> 00:45:05,995
Fine.

755
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:18,716
What do you want?

756
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:20,843
[grunts, cries out]

757
00:45:22,303 --> 00:45:24,013
[grunts]

758
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:26,224
[singer] ♪ I'm on the outside ♪

759
00:45:27,475 --> 00:45:29,310
♪ I'm on the outside now ♪

760
00:45:30,353 --> 00:45:32,230
♪ I'm on the outside ♪

761
00:45:33,272 --> 00:45:35,524
♪ I'm on the outside now ♪

762
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:38,527
-Thank you, make some noise!
-[♪ song ends]

763
00:45:38,611 --> 00:45:40,529
[partygoers cheering, applauding]

764
00:45:44,492 --> 00:45:46,160
[chattering, laughing]

765
00:45:51,165 --> 00:45:54,168
[♪ intense music playing]

766
00:46:08,975 --> 00:46:10,309
[partygoer screams]

767
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:13,938
[Bret] Susan and Robert were perhaps
the first teenagers in history

768
00:46:14,021 --> 00:46:18,234
to have their first kiss interrupted
by a scream heralding an attempted murder.

769
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:19,902
[♪ exciting music playing]

770
00:46:29,328 --> 00:46:31,497
[Liz gasps] Oh, my God!

771
00:46:36,711 --> 00:46:37,878
[Debbie gasps]

772
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:48,055
-Is he dead?
-[Steven] Looks that way.

773
00:46:48,139 --> 00:46:49,807
Looks like he slipped.

774
00:46:50,308 --> 00:46:52,226
Or crossed the wrong person.

775
00:46:58,107 --> 00:47:01,610
[sobbing] Daddy. Daddy, can you breathe?

776
00:47:02,653 --> 00:47:05,448
Please. Somebody call the police!

777
00:47:08,743 --> 00:47:10,077
Do something!

778
00:47:12,330 --> 00:47:15,875
Daddy, can you hear me? [crying]

779
00:47:22,506 --> 00:47:24,884
[phone ringing in distance]

780
00:47:30,222 --> 00:47:31,223
[officer] Wait here.

781
00:47:53,454 --> 00:47:55,039
Did you get any candy?

782
00:47:55,122 --> 00:47:56,207
What?

783
00:47:57,166 --> 00:47:58,376
At the Halloween party.

784
00:47:58,459 --> 00:48:02,046
I didn't see so much as a single M&M,
which was a total bummer.

785
00:48:02,129 --> 00:48:03,589
-Did you?
-Do you think you're being funny?

786
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:05,716
I'm sick of your sociopathic act, Robert.

787
00:48:06,634 --> 00:48:08,552
Terry Schaffer's on life support.
He could die.

788
00:48:08,636 --> 00:48:11,180
-Let me guess. You think I pushed him.
-Yeah, I do.

789
00:48:11,263 --> 00:48:13,682
Ever since you got to this town,
everything has gone sideways.

790
00:48:13,766 --> 00:48:14,767
My theory?

791
00:48:15,601 --> 00:48:17,812
Little birdie told me
Terry optioned your treatment.

792
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:20,439
Is that true?

793
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:23,609
Yeah. So?

794
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:27,071
What did you have to do
to get your big Hollywood break, Bret?

795
00:48:29,031 --> 00:48:32,284
I'm guessing… dark things.

796
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:34,829
Things you regret.

797
00:48:35,454 --> 00:48:36,831
Things you resent.

798
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:38,833
What time is your appointment?

799
00:48:39,792 --> 00:48:40,793
Why?

800
00:48:42,128 --> 00:48:43,629
No reason. [sighs]

801
00:48:44,588 --> 00:48:46,048
I just hope I go first.

802
00:48:46,966 --> 00:48:50,761
My evidence is indisputable.
You will be going away in handcuffs.

803
00:48:51,345 --> 00:48:53,097
If you go first,
it's gonna be nothing more

804
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,723
than a giant waste of everybody's time.

805
00:48:54,807 --> 00:48:55,975
I don't think so.

806
00:48:56,809 --> 00:48:59,103
I think if I go first,
you'll be hauled off to jail,

807
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,439
and then, inevitably,
comes the death penalty.

808
00:49:01,522 --> 00:49:03,232
-For what exactly?
-[Fregosi] You ready?

809
00:49:03,315 --> 00:49:04,400
Yeah.

810
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:08,320
-Well, follow me.
-[both] Which one of us?

811
00:49:09,447 --> 00:49:10,489
[chuckles]

812
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:12,408
Both.

813
00:49:13,993 --> 00:49:14,994
Now.

814
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:20,040
[♪ intense music playing]

815
00:49:20,124 --> 00:49:22,668
[Bret] What I didn't know then was
that life was about to cleave

816
00:49:22,751 --> 00:49:25,087
into a before and an after.

817
00:49:25,754 --> 00:49:27,965
And not just my life or Robert's,

818
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:31,760
but all of us.

819
00:49:41,687 --> 00:49:42,688
Sit.

820
00:49:45,232 --> 00:49:47,693
-Officers, I have some information about--
-[Donaldson] Just a moment, kid.

821
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:50,196
We're gonna get to individual interviews
in just a minute.

822
00:49:51,030 --> 00:49:53,240
[Fregosi] We've come into possession
of some evidence

823
00:49:53,324 --> 00:49:55,493
pertaining to the murders
of Katherine Latchford,

824
00:49:55,576 --> 00:49:58,746
Matt Kellner,
and the kidnapping of Rhonda Fox.

825
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:01,957
What… What sort of evidence?

826
00:50:02,041 --> 00:50:04,293
[Fregosi] We believe
all these crimes are connected.

827
00:50:04,376 --> 00:50:06,253
Committed by the same individual.

828
00:50:06,337 --> 00:50:08,506
And that individual is, uh…

829
00:50:09,215 --> 00:50:10,716
is someone in this room.

830
00:50:15,262 --> 00:50:16,347
I knew it.

